<title>USA: RDO Equipment share price jumps in debut.</title>
<headline>RDO Equipment share price jumps in debut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The share price of RDO Equipment Co jumped 2-3/8 points on their first day of trading, rising to 17-7/8 from their IPO price of $15.50 per share.$</p>
<p>Almost two million shares had changed hands by mid-morning, with the stock being one of the most active on the big board.</p>
<p>The company offered 4.2 million shares in a deal led by CS First Boston. The estimated pricing range was between $14 and $17 per share.</p>
<p>RDO, based in Fargo, N.D., owns and operates networks John Deere industrial and agricultural stores in the United States.</p>
